{"Title":"An Act relative to the expansion of the Good Samaritan law","BillNumber":"S985","DocketNumber":"SD40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T12:26:38.75"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T12:26:38.75"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S985/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Gobi, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 985) of Anne M. Gobi for legislation relative to the expansion of the Good Samaritan law.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 258C of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after Section 13 the following section:-\r\n\tSection 13A.  Any person who, in good faith, attempts to render care and assistance while in transit in a private vehicle to a person who is in need of care, and does so without compensation for the care from or on behalf of the person cared for, shall not be liable for acts or omissions, other than gross negligence or willful or wanton misconduct, resulting from the attempt to render such care and assistance.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}